{"catalog_digest":"816fe0b604d53f6a17c3889821d3e3c49d9cdf72cb86dcf77279098488a08dd0","composition_digest":"4f419cf9a5a1a35380ef9ce2dbf1452e9e1f8f137218053ac076174a389df77e","generation":"816fe0b604d53f6a17c3889821d3e3c49d9cdf72cb86dcf77279098488a08dd0","system_text":{"composition_digest":"4f419cf9a5a1a35380ef9ce2dbf1452e9e1f8f137218053ac076174a389df77e","item_digest":"7ab356879bd31a5af7b0899ff5c41c2d85ea663f35ec05f032a94db23e934726","preflight_digest":"c8e6d1dbf760bb325484d0a5c3ace6c8e52f3cb773d6d2f1e012750d3edb9512","text":"## Magic Context\n\n`ctx_search` searches this project's archive — what earlier sessions said and decided, commits and notes; ask it before asking the user anything that may already be recorded, phrased as a question with the exact names in it. `ctx_memory` pins facts that stay true for the months this work lasts, for you and every agent on the project: what must not have to be found again, especially what cost you turns. They are not shown to you automatically; recall them with `ctx_search`. `ctx_note` is the tray for work you intend to return to, with its findings attached; findings without an intention are not a note; \"take a note\" from the user always goes there.","tool_names":["ctx_memory","ctx_note","ctx_search"]},"tools":[{"capabilities":["magic-context:notes/v1"],"description":"Session notes are pending intentions: work you intend to return to, with findings attached (\"take a note\" always qualifies). Not active steps, an executing plan, or restart insurance; a record of how things stand (world-state, a design at a point in time) with nothing you intend to do about it — that goes stale silently; a fact worth keeping is memory, the rest is nothing. First line = title (<80 chars). write saves; read lists rows (note_ids for bodies); update changes one; dismiss retires 1–50. Dismiss a note when its work lands or is abandoned; a queue you never dismiss from stops being read. surface_condition parks it until an outside check against repo files, git, GitHub or the web holds.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"description":"write | read | update | dismiss.","enum":["write","read","dismiss","update"],"type":"string"},"content":{"description":"Note text: first line title (<80 chars), then detail.","type":"string"},"filter":{"description":"Read filter: all, active, pending, ready, dismissed. Omitted: active notes plus every current smart note (pending included); active: only active-status notes.","enum":["all","active","pending","ready","dismissed"],"type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Rows per read (default 25).","type":"number"},"note_ids":{"description":"One id for update, 1–50 for dismiss, or 1–50 to read those notes in full. Write and a plain read take an empty list.","items":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"maxItems":50,"type":"array"},"offset":{"description":"Skip newest rows (default 0).","type":"number"},"surface_condition":{"description":"A condition an outside checker can verify on its own, periodically (repository, releases, web — anything it can look up); never something only this conversation knows.","type":"string"}},"required":["action","content","note_ids"],"type":"object"},"name":"ctx_note","result_ops":["prepend","append"],"schema_digest":"cf84d0fffd0c46b40b50c6297d8d02f73ef5e0527f66cd14e24718ce1e3ef4f4","semantics":1},{"capabilities":["magic-context:memory.write/v1"],"description":"Durable facts about this project, shared with every agent on it and kept for the months this work lasts; active ones are already in <project-memory> as `#id: fact`. Write one standalone fact when it must not have to be found again — a rule, an architecture fact, a constraint, a config value, a naming convention — especially what cost you turns. A pending intention with evidence is ctx_note, not memory. write (content + category); update one id (content; category optional); archive one or more ids (reason optional); merge two or more ids (content); get 1–20 ids in any status.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"description":"write | update | archive | merge | get","enum":["write","update","archive","merge","get"],"type":"string"},"category":{"description":"Kind of fact (required for write; on update/merge pass the current category to keep it).","enum":["PROJECT_RULES","ARCHITECTURE","CONSTRAINTS","CONFIG_VALUES","NAMING"],"type":"string"},"content":{"description":"One standalone fact (write, update, merge).","type":"string"},"ids":{"description":"Ids from <project-memory>: one for update, 1+ for archive, 2+ for merge, 1–20 for get.","items":{"type":"number"},"type":"array"},"reason":{"description":"Why it is archived (optional).","type":"string"}},"required":["action","content","category","ids"],"type":"object"},"name":"ctx_memory","result_ops":["prepend","append"],"schema_digest":"de59b47f087c33bb84d20fe9eec0f5cdd5692089aa43e4bf19b72dcb53292cbc","semantics":1},{"capabilities":["magic-context:archive.search/v1"],"description":"Search available project memories, stored conversation, commits, primers and notes. Results are not filtered against visible context: this session has no compaction views. Phrase query as a natural-language question with exact terms you expect; a keyword stack finds less. Sources (omit for all): memory, message, git_commit, primer, note. Memory ids alone (`#7234`) resolve directly. from/to restrict every source to an inclusive UTC date range. History recovery requires active compaction and is not available in this tool set.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"from":{"description":"Earliest date, YYYY-MM-DD (inclusive).","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Maximum results (default 10).","type":"number"},"query":{"description":"A natural-language question carrying the exact terms you expect in the answer.","type":"string"},"sources":{"description":"Restrict to these sources; omit or [] for all.","items":{"enum":["memory","message","git_commit","primer","note"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"to":{"description":"Latest date, YYYY-MM-DD (inclusive; default open).","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"ctx_search","result_ops":["prepend","append"],"schema_digest":"36ed2de214be00f8a0a281dc7e6bb3da815b9da5c2a233b9c9006f148ee11561","semantics":1}]}